From: =?utf-8?b?T3R0byBLZWvDpGzDpGluZW4=?= <otto@debian.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Set git user.name in the system test

The system test sets 'git config --local user.email' but never a
user.name. git resolves the committer name from the GECOS field of the
current user and /etc/mailname, which is not always configured, e.g. in
CI containers. There git aborts with:

    fatal: empty ident name (for <entr.test@example.com>) not allowed

The warning is noisy and the failed 'git commit' makes the 'reverted
stash of files' test depend on unrelated fallbacks. Set an explicit
user.name alongside user.email so the test is self-contained.

Forwarded: no, should be
---
 system_test.sh | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/system_test.sh b/system_test.sh
index 96ebd04..4437433 100755
--- a/system_test.sh
+++ b/system_test.sh
@@ -403,6 +403,7 @@ try "exec single utility when an entire stash of files is reverted"
 		cd $tmp
 		git init -q
 		git config --local user.email entr.test@example.com
+		git config --local user.name "Entr Test"
 		git add *.h
 		git commit -m "initial checkin" -q
 		for f in `ls *.h | head`; do
